# Security Gate

- Never put secrets, API keys, private tokens, or credentials in client bundles or committed files.
- Validate and sanitize all user inputs and payloads before processing; prefer schemas (e.g. Zod) on boundaries.
- Prevent XSS: avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` / unsanitized HTML unless strictly necessary and sanitized.
- Protect auth surfaces: CSRF considerations where cookies/sessions apply; secure cookie flags; no auth tokens in localStorage unless an explicit secured pattern is chosen.
- Guard routes with server/middleware checks; do not rely on UI hiding alone for authorization (RBAC).
- Prefer a stable auth state API for UI: `user`, `isAuthenticated`, `isLoading`, `error`.
- Security Gatekeeper audits are read-only by default; apply security edits only when the user explicitly authorizes them.
